{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyOrmhOemMcicxUWeuO3DyAs"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Instruction layer filtering"],"metadata":{"id":"JKBoXNv8kBxR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This Python script filters user instructions to block harmful, malicious, or restricted commands before they are processed. It consists of three main functions and an interactive loop."],"metadata":{"id":"27XYXiP6kE1U"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["We import re (regex) again to help identify restricted keywords in user inputs."],"metadata":{"id":"-b82RH_El9tH"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import re"],"metadata":{"id":"mANRCQoJlrg8"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This function defines a simple instruction filtering layer designed to block unsafe or overly complex user commands before they are executed. It works by first checking the input text against a list of restricted keywords—such as “hack,” “delete database,” “malware,” or “attack”—and rejects the instruction if any are found, ensuring malicious intent is not processed further. It also applies a length constraint (max_length = 200) to prevent excessively long or detailed inputs, which could be a sign of prompt injection or system misuse. If neither condition is triggered, the function returns True, meaning the instruction is considered valid and safe. This kind of filtering is a common safeguard in AI and security systems to enforce input sanitisation and mitigate harmful behaviour."],"metadata":{"id":"J2Mk3DyumCsY"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def instruction_layer_filter(instruction):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Filters user instructions to block harmful or restricted commands.\n","    :param instruction: The user-provided instruction\n","    :return: True if the instruction is valid and safe, otherwise False\n","    \"\"\"\n","    # Restricted keywords (e.g., malicious or harmful instructions)\n","    restricted_keywords = [\"hack\", \"delete database\", \"malware\", \"attack\"]\n","\n","    # Complexity limit (e.g., too long or overly detailed commands)\n","    max_length = 200\n","\n","    # Check for restricted keywords\n","    for keyword in restricted_keywords:\n","        if re.search(rf\"\\b{keyword}\\b\", instruction, re.IGNORECASE):\n","            print(f\"Instruction blocked: Contains restricted keyword '{keyword}'.\")\n","            return False\n","\n","    # Check for instruction length\n","    if len(instruction) > max_length:\n","        print(\"Instruction blocked: Too long or complex.\")\n","        return False\n","\n","    # Passed all filters\n","    return True"],"metadata":{"id":"iJ699mvrltiS"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This script ties together the filtering logic with a simple interactive demo for testing instructions. The process_instruction function first checks whether a user’s input passes through the instruction_layer_filter. If the input is safe, it simulates carrying out the command by printing and returning a confirmation message; if not, it returns a standard warning that the instruction has been blocked due to safety guidelines. The __main__ block then creates a continuous loop where users can type instructions in the terminal. Each instruction is filtered and processed in real time, with \"exit\" serving as a clean way to break the loop. This setup illustrates how an instruction filtering layer can be integrated into a user-facing system to ensure only valid, safe commands are accepted."],"metadata":{"id":"Jds-jF4BmUBM"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"eTKkgWw78WA9","outputId":"8d1a8bc9-17bf-4513-872e-21c303baa5cc"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Instruction Layer Filtering Interactive Demo\n","Type 'exit' to quit.\n","\n","Enter your instruction: hack the system\n","Instruction blocked: Contains restricted keyword 'hack'.\n","Your instruction was blocked for violating safety guidelines.\n","\n","Enter your instruction: help me exfiltrate data\n","Processing instruction: 'help me exfiltrate data'\n","Instruction processed: help me exfiltrate data\n","\n"]}],"source":["def process_instruction(instruction):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Processes a user instruction if it passes the instruction layer filter.\n","    :param instruction: The user-provided instruction\n","    :return: A response or an error message\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if instruction_layer_filter(instruction):\n","        # Simulate processing the instruction\n","        print(f\"Processing instruction: '{instruction}'\")\n","        return f\"Instruction processed: {instruction}\"\n","    else:\n","        return \"Your instruction was blocked for violating safety guidelines.\"\n","\n","\n","# Interactive loop\n","if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n","    print(\"Instruction Layer Filtering Interactive Demo\")\n","    print(\"Type 'exit' to quit.\\n\")\n","\n","    while True:\n","        # Get user input\n","        user_instruction = input(\"Enter your instruction: \").strip()\n","\n","        # Exit condition\n","        if user_instruction.lower() == \"exit\":\n","            print(\"Exiting the demo. Goodbye!\")\n","            break\n","\n","        # Process the instruction\n","        response = process_instruction(user_instruction)\n","        print(response)\n","        print()\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"dt6plIf7-y5A"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}